Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: most important investment.

asr-000261
00:42:25.320 --> 00:42:25.880
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Mr. Speaker,

asr-000262
00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:28.360
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: this investment is already

asr-000263
00:42:28.360 --> 00:42:29.840
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: bearing fruit.

asr-000264
00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.280
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Two weeks ago, the Organization

asr-000265
00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:34.300
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: for Economic Cooperation and

asr-000266
00:42:34.300 --> 00:42:36.660
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Development released the results

asr-000267
00:42:36.660 --> 00:42:38.720
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: of the 2025

asr-000268
00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:40.420
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Program for

asr-000269
00:42:40.420 --> 00:42:42.260
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: International Student

asr-000270
00:42:42.260 --> 00:42:44.300
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Assessment, or PISA.

asr-000271
00:42:44.980 --> 00:42:46.440
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The Philippines recorded

asr-000272
00:42:46.440 --> 00:42:48.100
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: its strongest PISA

asr-000273
00:42:48.100 --> 00:42:50.380
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: performance since we first

asr-000274
00:42:50.380 --> 00:42:52.320
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: joined the assessment in 2018.

asr-000275
00:42:53.140 --> 00:42:54.520
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Our learners gained

asr-000276
00:42:54.520 --> 00:42:55.940
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: 20 points in reading,

asr-000277
00:42:56.540 --> 00:42:58.120
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: 17 points in science,

asr-000278
00:42:58.120 --> 00:42:59.980
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and 16 points in mathematics,

asr-000279
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: from the previous cycle.

asr-000280
00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:04.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: No participating country improved

asr-000281
00:43:04.000 --> 00:43:06.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: faster in reading than the Philippines.

asr-000282
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:12.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: And we were one of only eight education systems in the world

asr-000283
00:43:12.000 --> 00:43:16.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: to post significant gains in all three subjects.

asr-000284
00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:20.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: For the first time, the Philippines has moved out of the bottom 10.

asr-000285
00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:26.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: These are results of the reforms this House has funded in recent years,

asr-000286
00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:29.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and of the hard work of our teachers and learners.

asr-000287
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:30.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: But they are

asr-000288
00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: a starting point,

asr-000289
00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:34.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: not a finish line.

asr-000290
00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:36.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The gains we have made will only be sustained

asr-000291
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:38.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: if we continue to invest in

asr-000292
00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:40.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: the learners, the teachers,

asr-000293
00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:42.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and the classrooms that produce them.

asr-000294
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:44.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The budget before us today

asr-000295
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:46.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: is built to do

asr-000296
00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:48.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: exactly that.

asr-000297
00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:50.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Every peso we appropriate to this department

asr-000298
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:52.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: translates directly into

asr-000299
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:54.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: classrooms built, teachers

asr-000300
00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: hired and trained, learning

asr-000301
00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: materials produced, and most importantly,

asr-000302
00:43:58.000 --> 00:44:00.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: opportunities,

asr-000303
00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:04.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: given to more than 25 million Filipino learners

asr-000304
00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:06.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: across the country.

asr-000305
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:08.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Allow me, Mr. Speaker, to walk this Chamber

asr-000306
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:10.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: through the major items.

asr-000307
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: To promote the health,

asr-000308
00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:14.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: physical development, and learning

asr-000309
00:44:14.000 --> 00:44:16.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: readiness of Filipino learners,

asr-000310
00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:18.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: the sum of 11.4 billion

asr-000311
00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:20.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: has been allocated for the

asr-000312
00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: DepEd's school-based feeding program.

asr-000313
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:24.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: This appropriation

asr-000314
00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:26.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: shall support the provision of nutritious

asr-000315
00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: meals to public school learners

asr-000316
00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:30.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: with the objective of

asr-000317
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:32.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: addressing malnutrition,

asr-000318
00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: improving school attendance,

asr-000319
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:36.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and fostering an environment

asr-000320
00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:38.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: conducive to the physical and

asr-000321
00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:40.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: mental preparedness of every

asr-000322
00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:42.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: child to learn.

asr-000323
00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:44.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: To further expand access to educational

asr-000324
00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:46.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: opportunities, 38.12 billion

asr-000325
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:48.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: has been allocated for government

asr-000326
00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:50.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: assistance and subsidies.

asr-000327
00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: This funding

asr-000328
00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:54.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: will enable learners to access

asr-000329
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:56.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: quality basic education

asr-000330
00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:58.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: through both public

asr-000331
00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:00.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and private education providers.

asr-000332
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:17.380
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: In recognition of the vital role our educators play at the heart of a quality education system, 12.09 billion has been allocated to the Expanded Career Progression Program, enabling the promotion of qualified teachers.

asr-000333
00:45:17.380 --> 00:45:35.780
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Mr. Speaker, amid the recent unconscionable incidents of gun violence in various schools, the Department of Education remains committed to ensuring the safety and security of learners and personnel in all its campuses.

asr-000334
00:45:35.780 --> 00:45:43.140
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: In support of this commitment, the proposed budget provides for school safety and security for DepEd schools.

asr-000335
00:45:43.780 --> 00:45:47.140
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: This representation respectfully urges this august Chamber

asr-000336
00:45:47.380 --> 00:46:01.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: to give this allocation serious consideration and at the appropriate time to consider enhancing it further to mitigate and eventually prevent such painful incidents.

asr-000337
00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:11.240
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: In light of the foregoing, I respectfully request the support of my colleagues for the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Education.

asr-000338
00:46:11.860 --> 00:46:17.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: This budget will enable the Department to carry out its mandate and sustain its ongoing efforts

asr-000339
00:46:17.380 --> 00:46:31.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: to reform and improve basic education so that every Filipino learner may receive a quality education in a safe and conducive environment.

asr-000340
00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:32.280
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000341
00:46:32.960 --> 00:46:37.120
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: This representation is now ready to answer questions from our colleagues.

asr-000342
00:46:38.660 --> 00:46:41.100
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: Thank you, Honorable Zamora. Majority Leader.

asr-000343
00:46:41.100 --> 00:46:47.100
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Antonio Tinio of ACT Teachers

asr-000344
00:46:47.380 --> 00:46:49.180
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: to interpellate the sponsor.

asr-000345
00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:51.820
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: The Honorable Tino is now recognized.

asr-000346
00:46:52.280 --> 00:46:52.960
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: You may proceed, sir.

asr-000347
00:47:04.200 --> 00:47:05.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000348
00:47:09.300 --> 00:47:16.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, ang unang concern po natin, kaugnay sa budget ng Department of Education,

asr-000349
00:47:17.380 --> 00:47:30.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: proposed for 2027 ay yung mga cuts o pagbawas sa mga mahalagang programa nito.

asr-000350
00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:47.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung ikukumpara natin yung proposed budget for 2027 at yung budget ng DepEd

asr-000351
00:47:47.040 --> 00:47:48.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa General Appropriations Act.

asr-000352
00:47:49.440 --> 00:47:58.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, umaabot po sa 44.5 billion ang nabawas.

asr-000353
00:47:59.120 --> 00:48:06.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 44.45 billion ang nabawas sa budget ng Office of the Secretary.

asr-000354
00:48:08.140 --> 00:48:12.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, for example, ililista po natin

asr-000355
00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:16.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: as learner support programs

asr-000356
00:48:17.040 --> 00:48:22.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may bawas ng 1.8 million pesos.

asr-000357
00:48:23.660 --> 00:48:25.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isa-isa yun na natin.

asr-000358
00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:27.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi ko na ididetalye yung mga amounts,

asr-000359
00:48:27.580 --> 00:48:30.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: but there are cuts in the learner support programs,

asr-000360
00:48:31.540 --> 00:48:33.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in human resource development,

asr-000361
00:48:34.480 --> 00:48:37.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: physical fitness and sports.

asr-000362
00:48:38.660 --> 00:48:39.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me just highlight this.

asr-000363
00:48:39.900 --> 00:48:46.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: From 739 million to

asr-000364
00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:51.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 489 million. That is a 33.7% reduction.

asr-000365
00:48:51.520 --> 00:48:58.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For new school personnel positions,

asr-000366
00:48:59.740 --> 00:49:06.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: from 42.2 billion in 2026,

asr-000367
00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:10.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: naging 31.7 billion na lamang,

asr-000368
00:49:10.720 --> 00:49:15.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: that's a 10.5 billion reduction by one-fourth,

asr-000369
00:49:15.920 --> 00:49:16.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: reduction by one-fourth,

asr-000370
00:49:17.040 --> 00:49:23.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for flexible learning options.

asr-000371
00:49:24.660 --> 00:49:27.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nabawasan po by 1.06 billion.

asr-000372
00:49:29.120 --> 00:49:32.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The special needs education program

asr-000373
00:49:33.840 --> 00:49:37.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nabawasan ng 193 million,

asr-000374
00:49:38.100 --> 00:49:39.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 18% reduction.

asr-000375
00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:45.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isama natin ang

asr-000376
00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:46.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2017,

asr-000377
00:49:47.040 --> 00:49:57.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Child Protection Program, actually the item was removed. Wala nang budget for 2027.

asr-000378
00:50:00.760 --> 00:50:11.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The School-Based Feeding Program, nabawasan ng 11.4 billion pesos, a 55% reduction.

asr-000379
00:50:11.260 --> 00:50:27.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For the Indigenous Peoples Education Program, relatively maliit lang ang budget nito, 154 million in 2026.

asr-000380
00:50:27.440 --> 00:50:33.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now it's only 76 million, 78% reduction.

asr-000381
00:50:33.280 --> 00:50:41.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The Computerization Program, napag-uusap-usapan ito, yung pag-provide ng laptop sa mga tibig.

asr-000382
00:50:41.260 --> 00:50:50.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: From the current 10.6 billion to 5.7 billion, a 45% decrease.

asr-000383
00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:57.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Multi-Grade Education, cut by 61%.

asr-000384
00:50:58.260 --> 00:51:10.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Administration of Personnel Benefits, para sa mga binipisyo, from 8.4 billion to 5.2 billion.

asr-000385
00:51:11.260 --> 00:51:14.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Cut by 3.1 billion pesos.

asr-000386
00:51:15.740 --> 00:51:27.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, total po ng mga items, hindi pa nga lahat yun, ay 44.45 billion po ang nabawas sa programs.

asr-000387
00:51:28.720 --> 00:51:34.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At nakita po natin, mga major programs ito, sa ilalim ng Office of the Secretary.

asr-000388
00:51:35.260 --> 00:51:41.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang magiging epekto sa Department?

asr-000389
00:51:41.260 --> 00:51:53.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ano ang paliwanag ng sponsor kung bakit ito ang nais na ipasa na budget ng Department of Education?

asr-000390
00:51:53.640 --> 00:51:58.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Gayong napakalaki po ng mga bawas sa mga major na programa nito.

asr-000391
00:51:58.540 --> 00:52:09.540
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Sir Speaker, first of all, allow me to thank His Honor, Honorable Tinu for highlighting the...

asr-000392
00:52:11.260 --> 00:52:19.180
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Reduction as reflected from GAAA 2026 to NEP 2027.

asr-000393
00:52:19.820 --> 00:52:23.800
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: We, same with this sponsor, we acknowledge that reduction.

asr-000394
00:52:23.800 --> 00:52:36.800
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: But allow me to emphasize, Mr. Speaker, that based on the proposal of DepEd in NEP 2026, vis-a-vis the NEP of 2027,

asr-000395
00:52:37.180 --> 00:52:38.800
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: we have almost the same...

asr-000396
00:52:38.800 --> 00:52:39.800
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Same...

asr-000397
00:52:41.260 --> 00:52:43.180
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Proposal, almost the same.

asr-000398
00:52:43.180 --> 00:52:51.400
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: It's just that in GAAA 2026, this House has appropriated more than what has been proposed in NEP,

asr-000399
00:52:51.580 --> 00:53:00.660
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: with the acknowledgement of the members of the House of Representatives to give more support to the programs being mentioned by His Honor.

asr-000400
00:53:01.120 --> 00:53:09.260
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: At this point, since the Department of Education has proposed for the NEP 2027,

asr-000401
00:53:09.260 --> 00:53:19.880
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: it is also the hope of the Department that the members of this House of Representatives will also take note of what the Honorable Tinu has noted,

asr-000402
00:53:20.520 --> 00:53:29.000
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: the need for a more allocation for the programs being enumerated earlier.

asr-000403
00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:38.940
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The Department acknowledges that a lower budget will also affect the performance of the whole Department.

asr-000404
00:53:39.260 --> 00:53:54.740
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: But again, the Department leaves this to the members of this August body to give the appropriate support to be given to the Department, Mr. Speaker, Your Honor.

asr-000405
00:53:54.740 --> 00:54:08.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ang sabi po ng sponsor, Mr. Speaker, ay yes, bumaba, katulad nung binanggit natin, ang proposed funding for these major programs and projects.

asr-000406
00:54:09.260 --> 00:54:18.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, halos pareho lang daw kung ikukumpara ang NEP ng 2026 at NEP ng 2027.

asr-000407
00:54:18.060 --> 00:54:20.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So kongreso ang nagdagdag.

asr-000408
00:54:22.320 --> 00:54:28.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ngayon, ay tama po ba ang intindi ko, Madam Speaker, Mr. Speaker,

asr-000409
00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:37.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kumaasa ang DepEd sa kongreso para dagdagan ang mga pondo na ito? Tama po ba?

asr-000410
00:54:38.520 --> 00:54:39.140
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Mr. Speaker,

asr-000411
00:54:39.260 --> 00:54:49.540
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: That is accurate, Your Honor. May mga wish list po na gusto kong iparating ang ating Department sa mga membro ng kongreso.

asr-000412
00:54:50.020 --> 00:54:56.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So nakalimutan kang banggitin, mga significant cuts dito, for the record,

asr-000413
00:54:57.500 --> 00:55:08.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: national literacy policies and programs from 105.5 million, naging 15 million na lang, 15.3 million pesos.

asr-000414
00:55:09.260 --> 00:55:17.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That's a 90% reduction for 2027. Literacy, national literacy policies.

asr-000415
00:55:17.140 --> 00:55:27.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So this is meant to address the edcom finding, di ba?

asr-000416
00:55:27.220 --> 00:55:38.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na napakataas po ng functional illiteracy even among graduates of the basic education system.

asr-000417
00:55:38.500 --> 00:55:41.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And yet, binawasan ng 90% yung funding nito.

asr-000418
00:55:42.560 --> 00:55:50.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Textbooks and other instructional materials from 19.5 billion, naging 6.4 billion na lang po.

asr-000419
00:55:51.140 --> 00:55:57.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 66% reduction. Textbooks and other instructional materials.

asr-000420
00:55:57.580 --> 00:56:04.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang alam ko, Undersecretary Angara ay bumabawi na after more than a decade of

asr-000421
00:56:04.500 --> 00:56:05.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: minimal textbooks.

asr-000422
00:56:08.500 --> 00:56:11.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Textbook procurement ay pinabilis.

asr-000423
00:56:12.880 --> 00:56:16.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Finacilitate at nagpo-procure muli ng textbooks ang DepEd.

asr-000424
00:56:16.680 --> 00:56:17.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ano mangyayari?

asr-000425
00:56:18.280 --> 00:56:20.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Binawasan by 66% ito.

asr-000426
00:56:20.860 --> 00:56:27.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ngayon umaasa sa kongreso para maibalik.

asr-000427
00:56:28.220 --> 00:56:34.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po bang banggitin ng sponsor kahit yung mga pinakamahalagang,

asr-000428
00:56:35.120 --> 00:56:36.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sabi nyo may wish list ng DepEd.

asr-000429
00:56:36.980 --> 00:56:39.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwedeng marinig, for the record.

asr-000430
00:56:43.640 --> 00:56:45.160
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Mr. Speaker,

asr-000431
00:56:45.700 --> 00:56:52.220
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Gladly, this representation would like to manifest some of the wish list of the Department

asr-000432
00:56:52.220 --> 00:57:00.220
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: in order to carry out its programs and improve the performance of the Department.

asr-000433
00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:06.280
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Kasaama na dito ang mga dagdag na allocation

asr-000434
