06:29:58.920 --> 06:29:59.880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: dahil

asr-005999
06:30:00.000 --> 06:30:06.800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Karamihan po ng aking mga constituents na IPs ay nagpaabot po ng mensahe patungkol dito.

asr-006000
06:30:07.880 --> 06:30:13.460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can DA actually commit po to continue and support the 4K program?

asr-006001
06:30:15.060 --> 06:30:18.520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Rest assured po, I would like to also share, Mr. Speaker,

asr-006002
06:30:19.300 --> 06:30:24.640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: though mababawasan ang support ng nakalaan sa atin pong IPs because of the decrease in the NEP,

asr-006003
06:30:24.640 --> 06:30:30.880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: sa ngayon po, they are also being integrated, ang mga 4K sa mga banner programs ng DA.

asr-006004
06:30:31.180 --> 06:30:37.280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So despite the decrease in budget, we will do our best to assist them by integrating them into banner programs.

asr-006005
06:30:37.880 --> 06:30:41.720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Madam, our distinguished colleague and Mr. Speaker.

asr-006006
06:30:42.200 --> 06:30:45.040
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes, maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

asr-006007
06:30:45.480 --> 06:30:51.280
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ngunit gusto ko lamang pong ipaabot sa DA at sa aking mga colleagues na

asr-006008
06:30:51.980 --> 06:30:54.600
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: malugod po namin sinusuportahan ang 4K.

asr-006009
06:30:54.640 --> 06:31:04.640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dahil ang mga katutubong natulungan ng 4K program na ito ay masaya at mas lumalagot pa po ang kanilang negosyo.

asr-006010
06:31:05.600 --> 06:31:11.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kung ang balak po ng DA ay mawala po ang 4K program, ay sana po ay hindi.

asr-006011
06:31:11.260 --> 06:31:14.220
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Instead, this will continue in the near future.

asr-006012
06:31:15.040 --> 06:31:20.420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Speaker, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, before I proceed to my next topic,

asr-006013
06:31:20.420 --> 06:31:23.800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I wish to manifest my support for the continuation.

asr-006014
06:31:23.800 --> 06:31:26.560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and strengthening of the 4K program.

asr-006015
06:31:27.140 --> 06:31:33.880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nakikita po natin on the ground na ito ay tunay na nakakatulong sa ating IP farmers and fisher folks

asr-006016
06:31:33.880 --> 06:31:43.060
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at mahalaga na mapanatili at mapalakas po ang pondo para mas marami pang komunidad ang makinabang dito.

asr-006017
06:31:43.600 --> 06:31:51.800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At sana ay ibalik ang pondo na intended sa mga katutubong umaasang matulungan sa 4K program na ito.

asr-006018
06:31:51.800 --> 06:31:53.780
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor,

asr-006019
06:31:53.800 --> 06:32:00.380
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I will now proceed to my questions regarding the weather index-based parametric insurance.

asr-006020
06:32:01.420 --> 06:32:04.480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: In our consultations with farmers and fisher folks,

asr-006021
06:32:05.080 --> 06:32:12.140
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: we were informed that the DA-BFAR, in collaboration with the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation,

asr-006022
06:32:12.760 --> 06:32:19.400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: piloted a weather index-based parametric insurance for registered municipal fisher folk.

asr-006023
06:32:19.400 --> 06:32:25.880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ito ay isang klase ng insurance that pays a pre-agreed amount to beneficiaries

asr-006024
06:32:25.880 --> 06:32:33.120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: kagaya ng mga triggers, kagaya ng mga high wind speed or typhoon signal.

asr-006025
06:32:33.760 --> 06:32:36.460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: May I know any updates on this matter po?

asr-006026
06:32:37.680 --> 06:32:40.400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, I'd like to share the following updates.

asr-006027
06:32:41.080 --> 06:32:48.820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: In consultation, we were informed that the DABFAR and the PCIC are piloting, as you mentioned po,

asr-006028
06:32:48.820 --> 06:32:54.260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: a weather index-based parametric insurance for registered municipal fisher folks.

asr-006029
06:32:54.660 --> 06:33:03.240
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So they have already covered 14,215 fisherfolk in Occidental Mindoro, Antique, Cebu, Surigao del Norte, and Negros Oriental.

asr-006030
06:33:03.800 --> 06:33:12.660
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And they have a budget for 10 million, which will run from 2025 to 2026.

asr-006031
06:33:13.360 --> 06:33:15.440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They're also developing an actuarial model.

asr-006032
06:33:16.060 --> 06:33:17.920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, good sponsor.

asr-006033
06:33:17.920 --> 06:33:23.420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: My office also received information that local government units or LGUs

asr-006034
06:33:23.420 --> 06:33:30.380
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: that have been selected to pilot this insurance scheme from Negros Oriental and Surigao del Norte

asr-006035
06:33:30.380 --> 06:33:34.760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: have endorsed the continuation of the project in 2027.

asr-006036
06:33:35.600 --> 06:33:41.300
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Have you included in your 2027 budget the phase 2 of parametric insurance?

asr-006037
06:33:47.920 --> 06:34:02.780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes, we have included the 2027 budget.

asr-006038
06:34:03.580 --> 06:34:04.960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And how much do you think?

asr-006039
06:34:05.900 --> 06:34:07.060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker po.

asr-006040
06:34:07.520 --> 06:34:12.540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I'm sorry. Madam Sponsor, 10 million po yung kinakailangan para sa phase 2, tama?

asr-006041
06:34:14.640 --> 06:34:16.960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, yes, that is the needed budget.

asr-006042
06:34:16.960 --> 06:34:19.460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: For our targeted area.

asr-006043
06:34:19.920 --> 06:34:20.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po.

asr-006044
06:34:21.660 --> 06:34:31.660
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, I will now proceed with my questions na nais ipahatid ng aking colleague na si Representative Laila de Lima.

asr-006045
06:34:32.420 --> 06:34:41.780
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: This is regarding the Fisheries Administrative Order 266, yung Vessel Monitoring System and Electronic Reporting System po.

asr-006046
06:34:41.780 --> 06:34:46.780
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Noong January 21 of 2026, dineklara ng Supreme Court en banc

asr-006047
06:34:46.960 --> 06:34:56.760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: na unconstitutional ang FAO 266 na nagresulta sa pag-invalidate ng Mandatory Vessel Monitoring System

asr-006048
06:34:56.760 --> 06:35:03.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at Electronic Reporting System requirements para sa mga commercial Philippine flag fishing vessels.

asr-006049
06:35:03.900 --> 06:35:16.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang tanong ko, since ang VMS at ERS ay mahalagang tools para mamonitor ang fishing activities at ma-deter ang illegal, unreported, and unregulated,

asr-006050
06:35:16.960 --> 06:35:27.280
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: fishing, ano po ang naging kongkretong epekto ng Declaration of Unconstitutionality nito sa monitoring at enforcement efforts ng BFAR,

asr-006051
06:35:27.780 --> 06:35:37.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: particularly sa pag-pigil ng illegal fishing at protekta sa marine resources at kabuhayan ng mga munisipal fisherfolk?

asr-006052
06:35:39.000 --> 06:35:46.500
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, despite the nullification of FAO 266, the BFAR continues to implement Vessel Monitoring,

asr-006053
06:35:46.960 --> 06:35:51.140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: where it is required under the Philippines' international fisheries obligations,

asr-006054
06:35:51.800 --> 06:36:02.560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: including it as a condition for access to the waters of other coastal states and to fishing grounds managed by the regional fishing management organizations.

asr-006055
06:36:02.880 --> 06:36:14.620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, yes, humina po ang BFAR's enforcement capabilities, but they are still doing their best po.

asr-006056
06:36:16.960 --> 06:36:24.720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They retain alternative enforcement tools, including vessel inspection, sea patrol, onboard observers, etc.

asr-006057
06:36:24.940 --> 06:36:28.200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Marami po silang ginagawa, so we are happy to share that with you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-006058
06:36:28.840 --> 06:36:38.620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Following this ruling po, Madam Sponsor, ano po ang mga alternative systems o mechanisms na ginagamit ngayon ng BFAR to monitor fishing activities

asr-006059
06:36:38.620 --> 06:36:44.920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at maisagawa ang mga functions na dating sinasaklaw ng VMS at ERS?

asr-006060
06:36:44.920 --> 06:36:50.640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, the following po, Mr. Speaker, are occurring even as we speak.

asr-006061
06:36:51.100 --> 06:37:04.440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mandatory deployment of the MCS patrol boats, physical vessel inspections, sea patrols, onboard observers, logbook audits, port controls, licensing, intelligence gathering, at marami pa pong iba.

asr-006062
06:37:05.160 --> 06:37:06.960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

asr-006063
06:37:07.340 --> 06:37:13.240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: How many unregistered commercial fishing vessels have you identified in the entire country po?

asr-006064
06:37:14.920 --> 06:37:20.920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They recorded almost 2,500 registered vessels.

asr-006065
06:37:22.080 --> 06:37:23.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And how many have...

asr-006066
06:37:23.000 --> 06:37:24.400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yung mga unregistered?

asr-006067
06:37:24.540 --> 06:37:24.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes po.

asr-006068
06:37:26.380 --> 06:37:32.340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: How many have been apprehended by BFAR and what's the status of the cases filed against them po?

asr-006069
06:37:32.840 --> 06:37:34.920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ito po, i-share ko na lang po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-006070
06:37:35.440 --> 06:37:39.520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: 2025, 158, 2026, 76.

asr-006071
06:37:44.080 --> 06:37:44.880
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And magkano?

asr-006072
06:37:44.920 --> 06:37:54.300
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Magkano naman po ang nagastos ng BFAR para sa VMS at ERS bago ma-declare unconstitutional ang FAO 266?

asr-006073
06:37:56.720 --> 06:38:04.260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, total 3.440 billion from 2018 to 2026.

asr-006074
06:38:05.460 --> 06:38:12.280
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At may natitira pa po ba kayang funds ang BFAR para sa mga ito sa ilalim ng inyong 2026 budget?

asr-006075
06:38:12.280 --> 06:38:14.620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At meron pa po bang allocation?

asr-006076
06:38:14.920 --> 06:38:18.680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang mga ito sa 2027 proposed budget ng BFAR.

asr-006077
06:38:19.200 --> 06:38:27.440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: As of June 30, 2026, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, the remaining fund for the vessel monitoring system is 40 million.

asr-006078
06:38:28.000 --> 06:38:37.280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And for 2027, meron po tayong budget of 500 million for its operationalization and sustainability, Mr. Speaker.

asr-006079
06:38:38.240 --> 06:38:39.120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Maraming salamat po.

asr-006080
06:38:39.120 --> 06:38:44.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: On the DA budget and budget for production support services sub-program naman po tayo.

asr-006081
06:38:44.920 --> 06:38:52.620
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa fiscal year of 2027 NEP, isa ang DA sa mga department na may malaking budget cuts.

asr-006082
06:38:52.940 --> 06:39:02.920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: From 186 billion sa 2026 GAA, bumaba ito ng 15 billion at naging 171 billion sa 2027 NEP.

asr-006083
06:39:04.140 --> 06:39:14.120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Taon-taon sinasabi ng DBM na ang mga budget cuts na ito ay dahil sa poor absorptive capacity ng mga departments katulad ng DA.

asr-006084
06:39:14.120 --> 06:39:22.440
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang tanong ko po, one of the sub-programs ng DA na may malaking budget cut ang production supportive services sub-program.

asr-006085
06:39:23.160 --> 06:39:30.960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: From 35.6 billion sa 2026 GAA, bumaba ito ng 29.8 billion sa 2027 NEP.

asr-006086
06:39:31.660 --> 06:39:34.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: May 5.8 billion po ang naging cut.

asr-006087
06:39:34.900 --> 06:39:44.020
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa aming pagtingin sa NEP, nakikita po natin na ang production supportive services at nakalaan para sa iba.

asr-006088
06:39:44.120 --> 06:39:48.580
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang ibang uri ng crop production kasama na ang high value crops.

asr-006089
06:39:49.060 --> 06:39:53.480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Magkano po ang original proposal nito sa DBM para dito?

asr-006090
06:39:55.800 --> 06:40:03.880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Totally po, our 2027 proposal was 42B.

asr-006091
06:40:04.420 --> 06:40:10.360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Unfortunately, ang nalagay lang po sa 2027 NEP is 29.7B.

asr-006092
06:40:10.900 --> 06:40:12.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po.

asr-006093
06:40:12.100 --> 06:40:14.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano po ang konkretong implikasyon nito?

asr-006094
06:40:14.120 --> 06:40:19.240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa production capacity ng ating mga magsasaka at sa kanilang kita.

asr-006095
06:40:20.900 --> 06:40:27.180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, dahil nabawasan po ang area coverage para sa hybrid seeds,

asr-006096
06:40:31.280 --> 06:40:36.140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: halos nababalansi ito ng mga malawak sa inbred seed support sa ilalim ng RCEP.

asr-006097
06:40:36.480 --> 06:40:40.640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasabay nito, itinaas natin ang seedling rate support para sa hybrid rice.

asr-006098
06:40:41.280 --> 06:40:43.180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Gayunman, dahil walang pagpapataas,

asr-006099
06:40:44.120 --> 06:40:47.160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: sa kabuwang National Rice Program Budget Sealing,

asr-006100
06:40:48.200 --> 06:40:55.360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: yung ating nadagdag na seed support ay dapat tumbasan din po ng fertilizer allocation.

asr-006101
06:40:55.940 --> 06:41:02.880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So that is why we are requesting po for a larger fertilizer allocation which I read po earlier on.

asr-006102
06:41:03.160 --> 06:41:03.560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes po.

asr-006103
06:41:03.960 --> 06:41:08.480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano rin po ang nakikita ninyong posibleng impact nito sa presyo ng pagkain,

asr-006104
06:41:08.480 --> 06:41:13.480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: lalo na at nananatiling na sa 5.2% ang food inflation,

asr-006105
06:41:14.120 --> 06:41:18.080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: for July 2026, base sa datos ng PSA.

asr-006106
06:41:20.500 --> 06:41:25.760
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, well as we know po, rice plays a big role po sa ating inflation.

asr-006107
06:41:26.300 --> 06:41:32.160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And lalo na po, it's part of the talagang staple na binibili po ng mga Pilipino.

asr-006108
06:41:32.660 --> 06:41:39.000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So hopefully, hindi po tataas yung inflation due to the decreased budgetary support.

asr-006109
06:41:39.000 --> 06:41:42.960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: That's why we are urging po, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues,

asr-006110
06:41:42.960 --> 06:41:47.840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and our colleagues present here, to support the Department of Agriculture's budget.

asr-006111
06:41:48.280 --> 06:41:49.740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And kung pwede lang po, dagdagan pa.

asr-006112
06:41:50.500 --> 06:41:52.380
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

asr-006113
06:41:53.020 --> 06:41:56.460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, in closing,

asr-006114
06:41:57.100 --> 06:42:00.660
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: kung ang agrikultura ang pundasyon ng ating ekonomiya,

asr-006115
06:42:01.040 --> 06:42:05.960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang Pilipinas ay mananatiling gutom at mahirap kung babawasan natin ang suporta

asr-006116
06:42:06.540 --> 06:42:10.800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa ating mga magsasaka, mangingisda, at food producers.

asr-006117
06:42:10.800 --> 06:42:12.940
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang bawat pisong nawawala.

asr-006118
06:42:12.940 --> 06:42:19.180
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa pondo ng agrikultura ay direktang papatay sa kabuhayan ng ating mga local producer

asr-006119
06:42:19.180 --> 06:42:24.000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at mas magmamahal ang presyo ng pagkain ng bawat pamilyang Pilipino.

asr-006120
06:42:24.680 --> 06:42:32.160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Insya Allah, buong suporta sana ng Kongreso ang ating mga magsasaka, mangingisda, at suppliers.

asr-006121
06:42:32.800 --> 06:42:38.480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ito ang tanging paraan para magkaroon tayo ng sapat at murang pagkain para sa lahat.

asr-006122
06:42:38.480 --> 06:42:42.400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor, for yielding into my question.

asr-006123
06:42:42.400 --> 06:42:43.320
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-006124
06:42:43.320 --> 06:42:46.140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you also po, Mr. Speaker, and our distinguished colleagues.

asr-006125
06:42:50.060 --> 06:42:51.000
Deputy Speaker Jefferson F. Khonghun: Majority Leader.

asr-006126
