Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and to establish 23 police stations and buildings across various regions.

asr-007575
07:44:58.300 --> 07:45:23.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I likewise seek your support for the establishment of the PNP Counterterrorism Center, which will provide integrated capabilities in information and communications technology, cybersecurity, operational readiness, and other technical requirements for addressing evolving security threats.

asr-007576
07:45:23.780 --> 07:45:49.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I must emphasize that our country continues to face an increasingly complex and evolving security environment. Among these emerging concerns is the nihilistic violence extremism, which may exploit vulnerable communities and use both physical and digital spaces to spread violent ideologies.

asr-007577
07:45:49.380 --> 07:46:01.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We must therefore ensure that our police personnel are adequately equipped, trained, and capacitated to confront these emerging challenges effectively.

asr-007578
07:46:02.380 --> 07:46:07.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, public safety does not end with the police and the fire service.

asr-007579
07:46:07.920 --> 07:46:18.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The Bureau of Jail and Management and Penology has substantially reduced jail congestions and intensified greyhound operations.

asr-007580
07:46:19.380 --> 07:46:27.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Resulting in the confiscation of illicit cash, illegal drugs, electronic devices and gadgets, and deadly weapons.

asr-007581
