asr-007799
07:56:34.000 --> 07:56:35.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with the question?

asr-007800
07:56:35.440 --> 07:56:37.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Is it under the DIL?

asr-007801
07:56:37.420 --> 07:56:39.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There's so many attached agencies,

asr-007802
07:56:39.140 --> 07:56:40.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: so it's hard to...

asr-007803
07:56:40.800 --> 07:56:44.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: By the way, anyway, when you do a budget, you know, it's...

asr-007804
07:56:44.300 --> 07:56:46.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is the entire agency, including the attached agencies?

asr-007805
07:56:46.680 --> 07:56:48.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have created a lot already.

asr-007806
07:56:48.020 --> 07:56:48.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay.

asr-007807
07:56:48.920 --> 07:56:50.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Fire stations, police stations.

asr-007808
07:56:50.800 --> 07:56:52.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Assuming fire station.

asr-007809
07:56:52.680 --> 07:56:53.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Fire station.

asr-007810
07:56:53.720 --> 07:56:54.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Fire station, sir.

asr-007811
07:56:54.680 --> 07:56:57.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have created a lot of fire station,

asr-007812
07:56:57.280 --> 07:56:59.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but kung tinatangin niyo kulang pa,

asr-007813
07:56:59.480 --> 07:57:01.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: totoong pong kulang pa.

asr-007814
07:57:01.100 --> 07:57:05.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's why we are seeking our constituents,

asr-007815
07:57:05.820 --> 07:57:08.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I mean, our colleagues in Congress,

asr-007816
07:57:08.660 --> 07:57:10.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to help the BFP.

asr-007817
07:57:10.660 --> 07:57:12.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The collection of BFP is 4.5 billion,

asr-007820
07:57:14.280 --> 07:57:15.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: a year.

asr-007821
07:57:15.440 --> 07:57:19.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But DBM only approves 1 billion per year.

asr-007822
07:57:19.900 --> 07:57:22.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If we want to solve

asr-007823
07:57:22.820 --> 07:57:27.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the lacking fire trucks and the fire stations,

asr-007824
07:57:27.780 --> 07:57:31.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: all we are asking is just 80%

asr-007825
07:57:31.680 --> 07:57:35.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: of the year's collection by 2027,

asr-007826
07:57:35.960 --> 07:57:37.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: tapos na po lahat yan.

asr-007827
07:57:37.380 --> 07:57:38.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And the good thing is,

asr-007828
07:57:38.880 --> 07:57:41.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with a good secretary, John Vic Rimulla,

asr-007829
07:57:41.680 --> 07:57:44.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nilinis po yung BFP.

asr-007830
07:57:44.120 --> 07:57:47.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Even po ang examination is online na.

asr-007831
07:57:47.460 --> 07:57:48.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Even the procurement,

asr-007832
07:57:48.920 --> 07:57:51.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: they are studying a government-to-government

asr-007833
07:57:51.500 --> 07:57:55.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: procurement strategy with South Korea.

asr-007834
07:57:55.220 --> 07:57:59.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So mawawala na po yung mga nataong natin middleman

asr-007835
07:57:59.720 --> 07:58:02.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: or mga lagayan or corruption.

asr-007836
07:58:02.480 --> 07:58:04.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So once nanlalinis na po ito,

asr-007837
07:58:04.620 --> 07:58:08.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pagtungo na po tayo doon po sa government-to-government

asr-007838
07:58:08.180 --> 07:58:11.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: transaction para po mas maging transparent.

asr-007839
07:58:11.920 --> 07:58:13.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And even the government of Korea, sa account,

asr-007840
07:58:13.960 --> 07:58:17.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kasi may accountability also kung doon po tayo bibili

asr-007841
07:58:17.560 --> 07:58:19.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ng mga fire truck.

asr-007842
07:58:19.160 --> 07:58:25.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So we are asking our colleagues to help us with the DBM

asr-007843
07:58:25.780 --> 07:58:28.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: just to release what is rightfully

asr-007844
07:58:28.720 --> 07:58:31.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: for our Bureau of Fire and Protection.

asr-007845
07:58:31.720 --> 07:58:33.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007846
07:58:33.220 --> 07:58:35.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: By the way, before I proceed to my next question,

asr-007847
07:58:35.760 --> 07:58:39.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'd like to commend our good Secretary for eradicating

asr-007848
07:58:39.680 --> 07:58:42.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the rootless corruption in Bureau of Fire.

asr-007849
07:58:42.900 --> 07:58:43.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sir.

asr-007850
07:58:43.960 --> 07:58:45.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sir, saludo po ako sa inyo na talagang, yan po, isa

asr-007851
07:58:45.920 --> 07:58:48.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: kasi na biktima, mga kamag-anak

asr-007852
07:58:48.060 --> 07:58:49.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ko rin. Totoo po yan.

asr-007853
07:58:49.980 --> 07:58:52.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, thank you very much for your

asr-007854
07:58:52.060 --> 07:58:53.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: for your

asr-007855
07:58:53.820 --> 07:58:54.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: continuing

asr-007856
07:58:54.560 --> 07:58:57.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: eradicating, if not totally

asr-007857
07:58:57.920 --> 07:58:59.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: eradicated, yung corruption dyan.

asr-007858
07:58:59.460 --> 07:59:00.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So on behalf of Secretary

asr-007859
07:59:00.880 --> 07:59:02.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Rimulya, we would like to thank

asr-007860
07:59:02.820 --> 07:59:04.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kong Presley and stop asking.

asr-007861
07:59:08.640 --> 07:59:09.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Anyway,

asr-007862
07:59:09.540 --> 07:59:11.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'll move. Maybe this will be my

asr-007863
07:59:11.500 --> 07:59:12.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: last three questions.

asr-007864
07:59:12.560 --> 07:59:14.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, school

asr-007865
07:59:14.100 --> 07:59:16.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: shootings, firearm access

asr-007866
07:59:16.220 --> 07:59:18.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and prevention. Recent

asr-007867
07:59:18.020 --> 07:59:20.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: shooting incidents in Tacloban City

asr-007868
07:59:20.000 --> 07:59:22.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: in June, Zamboaga City

asr-007869
07:59:22.140 --> 07:59:24.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: in August, and Banga, South

asr-007870
07:59:24.020 --> 07:59:25.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Cotabato on September 18

asr-007871
07:59:25.620 --> 07:59:27.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: have raised questions

asr-007872
07:59:27.740 --> 07:59:29.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: regarding firearm

asr-007873
07:59:29.840 --> 07:59:31.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: access by

asr-007874
07:59:31.740 --> 07:59:33.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: minors. The reporting

asr-007875
07:59:33.660 --> 07:59:35.780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: of potential threats and

asr-007876
07:59:35.780 --> 07:59:37.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: coordination among schools,

asr-007877
07:59:38.220 --> 07:59:39.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: local governments,

asr-007878
07:59:39.880 --> 07:59:41.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and law enforcement agencies.

asr-007879
07:59:41.460 --> 07:59:43.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The South Cotabato incident

asr-007880
07:59:43.920 --> 07:59:45.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: is the thirdly

asr-007881
07:59:45.960 --> 07:59:48.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: deadly school shooting

asr-007882
07:59:48.060 --> 07:59:49.380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: reported in the

asr-007883
07:59:49.380 --> 07:59:51.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: country since June.

asr-007884
07:59:51.660 --> 07:59:53.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Question, in light of this recent

asr-007885
07:59:53.700 --> 07:59:55.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: incident, what has

asr-007886
07:59:55.900 --> 07:59:57.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the department identified

asr-007887
07:59:57.500 --> 07:59:59.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: as the principal areas

asr-007888
08:00:00.000 --> 08:00:08.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That may require strengthening in the prevention of and response to violent incidents in school.

asr-007889
08:00:11.240 --> 08:00:24.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, as much as I would like to answer, but I cannot divulge any specific because this is an ongoing investigation still.

asr-007890
08:00:24.720 --> 08:00:40.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, hindi po nagpapabaya ang ating DILG and in fact, nag-coordinate na po tayo sa DepEd, nag-coordinate rin po tayo sa DICT, and mag-coordinate rin po tayo sa DSWD.

asr-007891
08:00:40.520 --> 08:00:54.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, and punot dulo nito, yung pong sinasabi natin na matagal na natin pinag-uusapan na regulation, lalo na po ng Facebook, lalo na po ng META.

asr-007892
08:00:54.720 --> 08:01:05.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Na kailangan din po natin yung tulong po nila na i-take down itong mga sites na kung saan bini-brainwash ang ating pong mga kabataan.

asr-007893
08:01:06.460 --> 08:01:09.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, we are talking about the security of our kids now.

asr-007894
08:01:10.600 --> 08:01:14.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero, may ginawa na po ang DILG and PNP.

asr-007895
08:01:14.680 --> 08:01:23.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Safer school zones beyond the school gate, the DILG issued Memorandum Order Circular 2026.037.

asr-007896
08:01:23.080 --> 08:01:33.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: To strengthen safety in roads, sidewalks, pedestrian crossings, waiting areas, transport points, and loading and unloading areas immediately surrounding schools.

asr-007897
08:01:34.400 --> 08:01:36.240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Clear local accountability.

asr-007898
08:01:36.900 --> 08:01:40.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Puno baranggays, lead implementation at barangay level.

asr-007899
08:01:40.680 --> 08:01:44.740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: May training din po na ginagawa ang ating pong mga kapulisan.

asr-007900
08:01:44.740 --> 08:01:49.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, kailangan din po ang tulong ng DSWD.

asr-007901
08:01:49.660 --> 08:01:52.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Dahil alam po natin na mga minor de edad.

asr-007902
08:01:52.220 --> 08:01:59.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang mga tina-target na mga black sites operation na nagbi-brainwash po ng ating pong mga kabataan.

asr-007903
08:01:59.540 --> 08:02:01.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, we have to be very careful.

asr-007904
08:02:02.220 --> 08:02:04.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I think this is a social problem.

asr-007905
08:02:05.380 --> 08:02:08.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This is not only the problem of the DILG.

asr-007906
08:02:08.860 --> 08:02:11.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It is also the problem of the parents.

asr-007907
08:02:11.820 --> 08:02:15.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to be very much aware of what's happening now.

asr-007908
08:02:15.700 --> 08:02:19.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Especially sa mga sites na wala po tayong control.

asr-007909
08:02:20.000 --> 08:02:22.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's why Congress is crying.

asr-007910
08:02:22.220 --> 08:02:26.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Crafting, regulation, lalo na po sa meta.

asr-007911
08:02:27.000 --> 08:02:29.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And may ginagawa na rin po ang DICT.

asr-007912
08:02:29.980 --> 08:02:32.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, hindi naman po ako nagde-defend sa DICT.

asr-007913
08:02:32.900 --> 08:02:35.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, we are well much versed with the situation.

asr-007914
08:02:36.800 --> 08:02:40.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, ang masasabi po natin, hindi po natin ito pinapabayaan.

asr-007915
08:02:40.160 --> 08:02:48.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang alam lang po natin, yung tatlo na insidente na nangyari po sa Tacloban, Sambuanga, South Cotabato.

asr-007916
08:02:48.940 --> 08:02:52.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero, hindi nyo po naitatanong kung ilan na po ang nasalba po.

asr-007917
08:02:52.220 --> 08:02:53.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nang ating kapulisan.

asr-007918
08:02:54.300 --> 08:02:57.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: More than 40 na mga bata ang naisalba na.

asr-007919
08:02:58.380 --> 08:03:04.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because sa ating mga intelligence reports, na I cannot divulge kung saan po galing.

asr-007920
08:03:04.860 --> 08:03:10.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero may mga tumutulong po sa atin, sa ating pong pamilya sa DILG.

asr-007921
08:03:11.080 --> 08:03:14.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And the Secretary, John Vicrimulla, is on top of it.

asr-007922
08:03:16.700 --> 08:03:20.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

asr-007923
08:03:20.160 --> 08:03:21.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I agree with you 100%.

asr-007924
08:03:22.220 --> 08:03:24.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That these social platforms, malaking bagay.

asr-007925
08:03:25.240 --> 08:03:32.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In fact, during the budget of the ICT here, I was the one who made the deferment of their budget because of the metas.

asr-007926
08:03:33.500 --> 08:03:37.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Meta, social platforms, especially the Facebook, nagkaroon ng problema dyan.

asr-007927
08:03:38.460 --> 08:03:42.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in light of that, Mr. Speaker, I move to my next question.

asr-007928
08:03:42.920 --> 08:03:51.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In the South Cotabato incident reports, indicate that warnings have been communicated to other students before the shooting.

asr-007929
08:03:52.220 --> 08:04:00.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What mechanisms currently allow students, parents, and school personnel to report potential threats to the police?

asr-007930
08:04:00.600 --> 08:04:04.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And how are such reports assessed and acted upon?

asr-007931
08:04:05.080 --> 08:04:07.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, we have the 911, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007932
08:04:08.400 --> 08:04:11.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, kung may mga reports po tayo na nalaman, just dial 911.

asr-007933
08:04:12.740 --> 08:04:15.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ika nga po, 5 to 7 minutes, nandun na po ang ating kapulisan.

asr-007934
08:04:15.820 --> 08:04:20.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But again, mas kailangan pong paigtingin ang ating pangangampanya.

asr-007935
08:04:22.220 --> 08:04:26.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi lang po ng ating kapulisan, lalo na po ng ating komunidad.

asr-007936
08:04:27.160 --> 08:04:34.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Even our PTA, dapat imbelto po dyan, our teachers, our barangay officials, our local government officials.

asr-007937
08:04:35.100 --> 08:04:38.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, I've said, tulong-tulong po ang kailangan.

asr-007938
08:04:39.080 --> 08:04:41.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi po kakayanin ng ating kapulisan.

asr-007939
08:04:41.800 --> 08:04:52.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Lalo na wala pa po tayong yung iniingi po namin na counter-terrorism building na mag-equip ng ating mga data.

asr-007940
08:04:52.220 --> 08:04:56.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Para po ma-preempt natin itong mga ganitong mga pangyayari.

asr-007941
08:04:57.320 --> 08:04:59.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, we need to equip our police.

asr-007942
08:05:00.560 --> 08:05:07.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We need to equip our DILG family para po matugunan ang safety, lalo na po ng ating mga kabataan.

asr-007943
08:05:07.760 --> 08:05:12.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And just to add, Mr. Speaker, the deferment of DICT is not only about META.

asr-007944
08:05:13.040 --> 08:05:15.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think it's also the performance of DICT.

asr-007945
08:05:16.680 --> 08:05:18.780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's not only about META.

asr-007946
08:05:18.780 --> 08:05:21.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007947
08:05:22.220 --> 08:05:31.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How is the department coordinating with the Department of Education and local government units

asr-007948
08:05:31.120 --> 08:05:38.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: to establish clear protocols for preventing, reporting, and responding to serious threats in school?

asr-007949
08:05:40.180 --> 08:05:44.440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do you have a coordination with the Department of Education vis-a-vis to DILG?

asr-007950
08:05:44.440 --> 08:05:51.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As I've mentioned, it's not only DEPED, even DSWD, even barangay officials, barangay TANOD,

asr-007951
08:05:51.600 --> 08:05:52.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: even the mayors.

asr-007952
08:05:53.140 --> 08:06:01.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The police is training also the barangay TANODs, but we cannot go directly to the students since minor po sila.

asr-007953
08:06:01.860 --> 08:06:11.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, that's why it's an, well, call it interagency, but we need a composite team to address this issue, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007954
08:06:12.460 --> 08:06:13.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007955
08:06:13.740 --> 08:06:14.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

asr-007956
08:06:15.660 --> 08:06:20.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The proposed local government empowerment program receives 6.494

asr-007957
08:06:21.600 --> 08:06:23.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: billion.

asr-007958
08:06:24.040 --> 08:06:35.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: However, its 2025 disbursement rate was 69%, making implementation capacity an important consideration alongside the proposed allocation.

asr-007959
08:06:35.580 --> 08:06:46.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My question is, what prevented the local government empowerment program from achieving a higher level of disbursement in 2025,

asr-007960
08:06:47.180 --> 08:06:51.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and what has changed to support timely implementation in 2025?

asr-007961
08:06:51.600 --> 08:06:57.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Are we, Mr. Speaker, just for clarification, are we talking about LGSF?

asr-007962
08:06:57.740 --> 08:06:58.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, yes, okay.

asr-007963
08:06:59.220 --> 08:07:04.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Regarding LGSF, there are several issues.

asr-007964
08:07:05.880 --> 08:07:09.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The DBM released additional fund of SARO, it was late, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007965
08:07:10.500 --> 08:07:15.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The program appropriation on November 25 to 27, 2024.

asr-007966
08:07:15.160 --> 08:07:20.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And also, Mr. Speaker, nagkaroon din po tayo ng election ban,

asr-007967
08:07:21.600 --> 08:07:24.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: only allowed ongoing projects to continue implementation.

asr-007968
08:07:25.180 --> 08:07:26.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And plus, Mr. Speaker,

asr-007969
08:07:26.980 --> 08:07:33.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: compliances of required certificates from the national government agencies prior to the implementation.

asr-007970
08:07:34.740 --> 08:07:36.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, ito po yung nagkakos ng delay.

asr-007971
08:07:36.780 --> 08:07:39.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Minsan po, late yung pagbigay ng pondo,

asr-007972
08:07:40.120 --> 08:07:41.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nagkaroon ng election ban,

asr-007973
08:07:42.040 --> 08:07:46.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nagkaroon tayo ng bagong officials na kailangan po natin turuan po ulit.

asr-007974
08:07:46.280 --> 08:07:51.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, these are the reasons kung ano po yung bakit nandidelay.

asr-007975
08:07:51.140 --> 08:07:51.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But,

asr-007976
08:07:51.600 --> 08:07:53.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nangyari ba yung project?

asr-007977
08:07:53.540 --> 08:07:53.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes.

asr-007978
08:07:56.980 --> 08:07:59.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-007979
08:07:59.740 --> 08:08:06.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The proposed expenditure program of the Early Childhood Care and Development Council

asr-007980
08:08:06.620 --> 08:08:12.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: declines from 357 million to 124.2 million,

asr-007981
08:08:12.980 --> 08:08:15.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: a reduction approximately 65%.

asr-007982
08:08:16.280 --> 08:08:21.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Question, what explains this reduction and what effect will it have?

asr-007983
08:08:21.600 --> 08:08:25.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: On support for early childhood services delivered through local governments.

asr-007984
08:08:27.080 --> 08:08:30.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, but we have to look at the data, Mr. Speaker.

asr-007985
08:08:31.360 --> 08:08:36.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As of June 2026, obligation rate was 45.56%.

asr-007986
08:08:36.080 --> 08:08:39.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As of June, this percent rate also,

asr-007987
08:08:41.840 --> 08:08:44.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2026 is 94.58%.

asr-007988
08:08:44.700 --> 08:08:47.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Comparing to the obligation rate,

asr-007989
08:08:48.180 --> 08:08:50.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: noong 2025, 92.09.

asr-007990
08:08:51.600 --> 08:08:57.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2025, disbursement rate, 72.7%.

asr-007991
08:08:57.440 --> 08:09:02.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And under the new law,

asr-007992
08:09:03.660 --> 08:09:05.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the establishment of NCDCs,

asr-007993
08:09:07.380 --> 08:09:08.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: tinanggal na.

asr-007994
08:09:08.440 --> 08:09:09.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kaya wala na pong infrastructure.

asr-007995
08:09:11.780 --> 08:09:15.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay, thank you very much, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-007996
08:09:16.820 --> 08:09:20.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Which functions and outputs will continue

asr-008001
08:09:21.380 --> 08:09:24.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And which will be reduced, transferred, or discontinued?

asr-008002
08:09:25.820 --> 08:09:27.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you repeat, Mr. Speaker, again?

asr-008003
08:09:28.180 --> 08:09:31.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Which functions and outputs will continue

asr-008004
08:09:31.980 --> 08:09:37.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: with regard to this early childhood care and development council

asr-008005
08:09:37.100 --> 08:09:38.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: because of declines?

asr-008006
08:09:39.200 --> 08:09:43.520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And which will be reduced, transferred, or discontinued?

asr-008007
08:09:46.520 --> 08:09:51.360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang trabaho po talaga ng ECCDC is ensuring the quality of care.

asr-008008
08:09:51.360 --> 08:09:52.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang trabaho po talaga ng ECCDC is ensuring the quality of education.

asr-008009
08:09:53.200 --> 08:09:59.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And coordination sa integrated ECCD program

asr-008010
08:09:59.440 --> 08:10:03.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: on health nutrition with the local government units.

asr-008011
08:10:04.640 --> 08:10:06.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So yun na po yung naging mandato niya.

asr-008012
08:10:07.340 --> 08:10:10.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So yung katanungan niya po kung sino po ang magpapatayo,

asr-008013
08:10:11.640 --> 08:10:14.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: well, it is my belief na

asr-008014
08:10:14.140 --> 08:10:18.400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: local government, pwede po.

asr-008015
08:10:18.840 --> 08:10:20.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Paranggay, pwede po.

asr-008016
08:10:20.040 --> 08:10:22.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congreso, pwede rin po.

asr-008017
08:10:23.600 --> 08:10:25.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So yung pagtulong-tulungan po natin.

asr-008018
08:10:25.560 --> 08:10:27.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero since bago na po yung mandate

asr-008019
08:10:27.520 --> 08:10:31.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na nakasaad sa batas,

asr-008020
08:10:31.640 --> 08:10:34.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: mas more of nakatutok na po sa quality of education

asr-008021
08:10:34.620 --> 08:10:36.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na tinuturo sa ating mga kabataan.

asr-008022
08:10:37.480 --> 08:10:39.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Disponsor.

asr-008023
08:10:40.720 --> 08:10:43.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What minimum national support is necessary

asr-008024
08:10:43.820 --> 08:10:46.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: to maintain service standards,

asr-008025
08:10:46.520 --> 08:10:49.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: particularly in poorer and geographically

asr-008026
08:10:49.040 --> 08:10:51.380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: isolated communities?

asr-008027
08:10:54.720 --> 08:10:58.740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, can I be more clarified?

asr-008028
08:10:59.020 --> 08:11:02.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's under, same, with regard to the early childhood care

asr-008029
08:11:02.900 --> 08:11:03.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and development.

asr-008030
08:11:04.000 --> 08:11:06.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We're talking about chichos, yung malalayo.

asr-008031
08:11:06.820 --> 08:11:07.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ah, yung malalayo.

asr-008032
08:11:07.800 --> 08:11:08.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes.

asr-008033
08:11:08.680 --> 08:11:10.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Paano nyo na ni-deliver doon?

asr-008034
08:11:10.800 --> 08:11:12.380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah, in the urban areas.

asr-008035
08:11:12.380 --> 08:11:15.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It is part of the mandate, whatever area it is,

asr-008036
08:11:15.040 --> 08:11:18.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: it's a mandate of the ECCDC, Mr. Speaker,

asr-008037
08:11:19.040 --> 08:11:20.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kahit po malayo pa yung lugar,

asr-008038
08:11:20.760 --> 08:11:22.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kahit po kailangan mawangka sila,

asr-008039
08:11:22.840 --> 08:11:23.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kailangan po nilang puntahan.

asr-008040
08:11:24.060 --> 08:11:25.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At kung may report po sa inyo

asr-008041
08:11:25.840 --> 08:11:28.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na hindi nila napupuntahan,

asr-008042
08:11:28.360 --> 08:11:31.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kindly tell Disponsor,

asr-008043
08:11:32.940 --> 08:11:34.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ako po mismo, sasamahan ko sila,

asr-008044
08:11:34.700 --> 08:11:35.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: puntahan yung mga lugar niyon.

asr-008045
08:11:36.380 --> 08:11:38.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's why I like this guy, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008046
08:11:39.100 --> 08:11:41.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tomorrow is our energy again.

asr-008047
08:11:41.380 --> 08:11:42.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, maraming salamat po.

asr-008048
08:11:42.860 --> 08:11:44.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I support the budget of DILG

asr-008049
08:11:44.840 --> 08:11:46.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: to the entire family of DILG.

asr-008050
08:11:46.800 --> 08:11:47.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you very much.

asr-008051
08:11:48.160 --> 08:11:48.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-008052
08:11:49.040 --> 08:11:50.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008053
08:11:54.040 --> 08:11:57.040
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Thank you, Honorable De Jesus. Majority Leader.

asr-008054
08:11:57.040 --> 08:12:01.040
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Mr. Speaker, next to interpellate the sponsor,

asr-008055
08:12:01.040 --> 08:12:04.040
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I move to recognize Representative Robert Nazal

asr-008056
08:12:04.040 --> 08:12:07.040
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: of BH Party-list.

asr-008057
08:12:07.040 --> 08:12:10.040
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Honorable Robert Nazal is recognized.

asr-008058
08:12:10.040 --> 08:12:12.040
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Please proceed.

asr-008059
08:12:12.040 --> 08:12:14.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008060
08:12:14.040 --> 08:12:16.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good afternoon, distinguished colleague.

asr-008061
08:12:16.040 --> 08:12:18.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good afternoon to the DILG.

asr-008062
08:12:18.040 --> 08:12:21.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I'd like to go to my first question.

asr-008063
08:12:21.040 --> 08:12:23.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, through you,

asr-008064
08:12:23.040 --> 08:12:26.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: may I ask our distinguished colleague

asr-008065
08:12:26.040 --> 08:12:28.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: to confirm with DILG

asr-008066
08:12:28.040 --> 08:12:32.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: how seriously are we monitoring LGU compliance

asr-008067
08:12:32.040 --> 08:12:35.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: with the expanded Solo Parents Welfare Act?

asr-008068
08:12:35.040 --> 08:12:38.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We continue to receive many complaints

asr-008069
08:12:38.040 --> 08:12:39.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: from solo parents

asr-008070
08:12:39.040 --> 08:12:41.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: that the benefits are provided by law,

asr-008071
08:12:41.040 --> 08:12:44.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: pero pagdating po sa LGU,

asr-008072
08:12:44.040 --> 08:12:46.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: hindi naman nila nakukuha,

asr-008073
08:12:46.040 --> 08:12:47.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: particularly the subsidy

asr-008074
08:12:47.040 --> 08:12:51.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and the implementation of the solo parent booklet.

asr-008075
08:12:51.040 --> 08:12:54.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So ang tanong ko po,

asr-008076
08:12:54.040 --> 08:12:56.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: how many LGUs are actually providing

asr-008077
08:12:56.040 --> 08:12:58.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: the 1,000 monthly subsidy

asr-008078
08:12:58.040 --> 08:13:00.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: to qualified solo parents?

asr-008079
08:13:00.040 --> 08:13:03.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how many qualified solo parents

asr-008080
08:13:03.040 --> 08:13:05.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: are actually receiving it today?

asr-008081
08:13:07.040 --> 08:13:10.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you for that, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008082
08:13:10.040 --> 08:13:12.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But to clarify lang po,

asr-008083
08:13:12.040 --> 08:13:14.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: hindi lang po trabaho ng DILG yan.

asr-008084
08:13:14.040 --> 08:13:16.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There's a joint circular na kasama po dyan,

asr-008085
08:13:16.040 --> 08:13:18.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ang DSWD,

asr-008086
08:13:18.040 --> 08:13:20.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: regarding the solo parent.

asr-008087
08:13:20.040 --> 08:13:22.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, regards to the question,

asr-008088
08:13:22.040 --> 08:13:25.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: total na...

asr-008089
08:13:36.040 --> 08:13:39.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, can I be clarified with the question again?

asr-008090
08:13:39.040 --> 08:13:42.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ilan pong LGUs ang actual na nag-proprovide

asr-008091
08:13:42.040 --> 08:13:44.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ng 1,000 per month subsidy?

asr-008092
08:13:44.040 --> 08:13:45.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi, actually,

asr-008093
08:13:45.040 --> 08:13:50.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: hindi rin po obligasyon ito ng DSWD.

asr-008094
08:13:50.040 --> 08:13:51.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, yes.

asr-008095
08:13:51.040 --> 08:13:54.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Siyempre, the LGUs are under the DILG.

asr-008096
08:13:54.040 --> 08:13:57.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, even given the circular,

asr-008097
08:13:57.040 --> 08:14:00.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ang nagmamonitor po dapat nung

asr-008098
08:14:00.040 --> 08:14:02.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: implementation ng LGU

asr-008099
08:14:02.040 --> 08:14:04.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: is DILG.

asr-008100
08:14:04.040 --> 08:14:06.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, ang tanong ko po is,

asr-008101
08:14:06.040 --> 08:14:10.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ilan po ang LGUs that are providing

asr-008102
08:14:10.040 --> 08:14:12.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: the 1,000 per month subsidy

asr-008103
08:14:12.040 --> 08:14:14.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and how many qualified solo parents

asr-008104
08:14:14.040 --> 08:14:16.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: are actually receiving it today?

asr-008105
08:14:16.040 --> 08:14:18.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, that is a very good question,

asr-008106
08:14:18.040 --> 08:14:19.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but as of now, Mr. Speaker,

asr-008107
08:14:19.040 --> 08:14:23.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I would like to apologize, indulgence.

asr-008108
08:14:23.040 --> 08:14:26.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Napakalawak po, but I totally agree with you.

asr-008109
08:14:26.040 --> 08:14:29.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And galing rin po ako sa LGU,

asr-008110
08:14:29.040 --> 08:14:31.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: although may autonomy po ang LGU,

asr-008111
08:14:31.040 --> 08:14:33.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but nasa mandato rin po yan

asr-008112
08:14:33.040 --> 08:14:35.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: sa local government code,

asr-008113
08:14:35.040 --> 08:14:37.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nalagyan po ng pondo,

asr-008114
08:14:37.040 --> 08:14:39.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo na sa mga single parents.

asr-008115
08:14:39.040 --> 08:14:41.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes, and this is a national law.

asr-008116
08:14:41.040 --> 08:14:42.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If I may, Mr. Speaker,

asr-008117
08:14:42.040 --> 08:14:45.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: can I give the data?

asr-008118
08:14:48.040 --> 08:14:49.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I-submit na lang po.

asr-008119
08:14:49.040 --> 08:14:50.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I-submit na lang po.

asr-008120
08:14:50.040 --> 08:14:51.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: In the previous hearing,

asr-008121
08:14:51.040 --> 08:14:53.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: we asked the DILG to study

asr-008122
08:14:53.040 --> 08:14:54.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: whether actual compliance

asr-008123
08:14:54.040 --> 08:14:57.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: with the Solo Parents' Welfare Act

asr-008124
08:14:57.040 --> 08:15:00.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: can be incorporated into the seal.

asr-008125
08:15:00.000 --> 08:15:07.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: of good local governance and DILG promised that they would study it, ano po ang naging resulta nito?

asr-008126
08:15:07.900 --> 08:15:13.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And can DILG commit today to actual implementation?

asr-008127
08:15:14.040 --> 08:15:20.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: At pwede na po bang isama sa seal of good governance ang compliance nito?

asr-008128
08:15:20.800 --> 08:15:24.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, actually yan na po yung ginagawa po ng DILG.

asr-008129
08:15:25.020 --> 08:15:29.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi lang po ang pag-aral nito, hindi kung paano na po isagawa po ito.

asr-008130
08:15:29.020 --> 08:15:33.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, duly noted ang magandang suggestion ng ating butihin na.

asr-008131
08:15:33.600 --> 08:15:40.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, is there, can DILG commit to a date or kung kailan po natin pwedeng i-implement?

asr-008132
08:15:40.200 --> 08:15:49.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kahit yung isama lang po sa seal of good governance itong implementation ng Solo Parents Welfare Act.

asr-008133
08:15:49.500 --> 08:15:57.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nasa TWG na po ito. So, hopefully within siguro, I think a month, ano po, I think in one month,

asr-008134
08:15:58.040 --> 08:15:59.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: makakalabas na po.

asr-008135
08:15:59.020 --> 08:16:03.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, mayroon po sila ng bagong regulasyon tungkol po dito.

asr-008136
08:16:04.200 --> 08:16:06.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Okay. Thank you for that, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-008137
08:16:06.380 --> 08:16:09.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, we have a commitment from DILG na lalabas na po ito?

asr-008138
08:16:09.780 --> 08:16:14.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, but Mr. Speaker, kahit ilabas po ito, ang timeline po natin is for next year.

asr-008139
08:16:15.900 --> 08:16:17.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we have a date kung...

asr-008140
08:16:17.920 --> 08:16:18.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next year, January.

asr-008141
08:16:19.700 --> 08:16:21.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-008142
08:16:22.200 --> 08:16:26.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And may we request the DILG to regularly furnish the office of this representation,

asr-008143
08:16:27.140 --> 08:16:28.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: preferably quarterly.

asr-008144
08:16:29.020 --> 08:16:32.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We have a status of LGU compliant, so we can follow up on non-compliant LGUs.

asr-008145
08:16:32.800 --> 08:16:34.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Para matulungan din po namin kayo.

asr-008146
08:16:34.340 --> 08:16:36.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, duly noted, and thank you for that.

asr-008147
08:16:37.540 --> 08:16:43.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: My next question, Distinguished Colleague, Mr. Speaker, is on the Unified 9-1-1.

asr-008148
08:16:46.040 --> 08:16:57.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, through you, COA found that the 9-1-1 Emergency Services Program had an obligation rate of only 2.45% in 2025.

asr-008149
08:16:57.180 --> 08:16:58.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, please.

asr-008150
08:16:59.020 --> 08:17:01.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: May I ask, bakit po 2.45% lang?

asr-008151
08:17:02.640 --> 08:17:04.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What specifically was not implemented?

asr-008152
08:17:05.640 --> 08:17:07.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what has changed since then?

asr-008153
08:17:12.780 --> 08:17:15.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you repeat the question again? I'm sorry.

asr-008154
08:17:16.040 --> 08:17:26.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yung ano po, COA found that the 9-1-1 Emergency Services Program had an obligation rate of only 2.45% in 2025.

asr-008155
08:17:26.900 --> 08:17:29.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, the question is, bakit po 2.45% na ito?

asr-008156
08:17:29.000 --> 08:17:30.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Bakit 2.45% lang?

asr-008157
08:17:31.620 --> 08:17:33.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What specifically was not implemented?

asr-008158
08:17:34.600 --> 08:17:36.600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what has changed since then?

asr-008159
08:17:38.120 --> 08:17:45.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I think the problem was the vehicles, Mr. Speaker, but we have updated it already.

asr-008160
08:17:46.620 --> 08:17:51.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, sigurado po, mas matasa po yan ngayon, based on the data sa 2025.

asr-008161
08:17:52.280 --> 08:17:56.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, for 2025 po and 2026, magkano po ang na-appropriate?

asr-008162
08:17:56.860 --> 08:17:58.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yung na-release?

asr-008163
08:17:59.000 --> 08:18:03.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Na-obligate and was actually disbursed for Unified 9-1-1?

asr-008164
08:18:03.980 --> 08:18:06.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: For 2025, it's only 1 billion.

asr-008165
08:18:07.500 --> 08:18:08.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For 2026?

asr-008166
08:18:08.500 --> 08:18:08.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: For 2026.

asr-008167
08:18:08.880 --> 08:18:11.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Appropriated, released, obligated, and actually disbursed.

asr-008168
08:18:11.720 --> 08:18:13.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, disbursement na yan lang.

asr-008169
08:18:14.700 --> 08:18:25.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That was allocated, but the disbursement is around 1.4 billion for 2025.

asr-008170
08:18:25.120 --> 08:18:28.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: For both 2025 and

asr-008171
08:18:29.000 --> 08:18:30.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2026, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008172
08:18:31.400 --> 08:18:33.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-008173
08:18:34.220 --> 08:18:39.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can our Distinguished Colleague break down the spending, how much went to the technology platform,

asr-008174
08:18:40.360 --> 08:18:48.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and private service providers, command centers, and telecommunications, ambulances, and other vehicles, personnel, and training?

asr-008175
08:18:48.760 --> 08:18:51.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker, can we submit?

asr-008176
08:18:52.380 --> 08:18:55.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Since marami po ito, if you can give us time.

asr-008177
08:18:56.040 --> 08:18:56.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Siguro po.

asr-008178
08:18:56.700 --> 08:18:57.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: By today?

asr-008179
08:18:59.000 --> 08:19:02.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Isasubmit po natin sa ating pong colleague.

asr-008180
08:19:03.000 --> 08:19:04.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-008181
08:19:05.740 --> 08:19:13.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can our Distinguished Colleague also confirm that 9-11 is completely free to the public?

asr-008182
08:19:13.700 --> 08:19:16.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And on the government side, what are we paying annually?

asr-008183
08:19:17.240 --> 08:19:23.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Including recurring service, technology, telecommunications, or other fees to operate Unified 9-1-1?

asr-008184
08:19:25.160 --> 08:19:27.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Free po yung call ng public.

asr-008185
08:19:28.440 --> 08:19:28.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, siyempre po,

asr-008186
08:19:29.000 --> 08:19:30.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: may gaso simpo sa government.

asr-008187
08:19:31.960 --> 08:19:33.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It's because of the system.

asr-008188
08:19:33.900 --> 08:19:34.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes, of course.

asr-008189
08:19:34.300 --> 08:19:36.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But to call for the public, it's free.

asr-008190
08:19:36.640 --> 08:19:37.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 100% free.

asr-008191
08:19:37.740 --> 08:19:41.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can I also get a report on papano po ito nadi-disperse?

asr-008192
08:19:42.000 --> 08:19:43.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Papano siya hinahati-hati?

asr-008193
08:19:43.700 --> 08:19:47.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, we will submit by today, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008194
08:19:47.300 --> 08:19:50.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Colleague, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008195
08:19:51.500 --> 08:19:56.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: May I ask, how many genuine emergencies resulted in an actual dispatch?

asr-008196
08:19:56.580 --> 08:19:58.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what is the average response?

asr-008197
08:19:59.000 --> 08:20:06.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: From receipt of a 9-1-1 call, not merely until somebody answers this phone, the telephone,

asr-008198
08:20:06.820 --> 08:20:10.740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but until the appropriate responder physically arrives at the scene?

asr-008199
08:20:11.800 --> 08:20:15.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The average response time is 5 to 7 minutes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008200
08:20:17.960 --> 08:20:22.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we measure how many patients were successfully assisted or stabilized?

asr-008201
08:20:22.900 --> 08:20:26.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How many emergencies were resolved through timely intervention?

asr-008202
08:20:27.900 --> 08:20:28.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008203
08:20:28.440 --> 08:20:28.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And where?

asr-008204
08:20:29.000 --> 08:20:34.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Measurable how many lives were saved because of a timely 9-1-1 response?

asr-008205
08:20:35.280 --> 08:20:36.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008206
08:20:36.200 --> 08:20:41.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We just have to pull up the data and submit to our colleague, Congressman Robert Nazal.

asr-008207
08:20:41.960 --> 08:20:49.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But definitely, alam po yan ng ating pong 9-1-1 responders.

asr-008208
08:20:49.480 --> 08:20:50.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Siyempre po, hindi po.

asr-008209
08:20:50.500 --> 08:20:57.360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, just for example, ito po.

asr-008210
08:20:57.360 --> 08:21:13.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, from September 11, 2025 to July 31, 2026, the National Call Center recorded 14,461,871 incoming calls.

asr-008211
08:21:17.520 --> 08:21:22.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 13,931,388 handled calls.

asr-008212
08:21:23.680 --> 08:21:27.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 96.33% handling efficiency.

asr-008213
08:21:27.360 --> 08:21:32.360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 513,483 abandoned calls.

asr-008214
08:21:33.100 --> 08:21:38.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And 17,469 documented prank calls.

asr-008215
08:21:39.520 --> 08:21:44.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The volume is approximately 53,000 incoming calls per day.

asr-008216
08:21:45.440 --> 08:21:51.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ilan po yung actual na-save natin dun sa mga totoong may emergency?

asr-008217
08:21:51.200 --> 08:21:57.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung handled calls is 13,000,000.

asr-008218
08:21:57.360 --> 08:21:59.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 13,931,388.

asr-008219
08:22:00.420 --> 08:22:06.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Out of the 14,461,871 incoming calls.

asr-008220
08:22:06.820 --> 08:22:11.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, 96.33 handling efficiency po tayo.

asr-008221
08:22:14.100 --> 08:22:22.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can a measurable emergency outcome become an actual performance indicator tied to 9-1-1?

asr-008222
08:22:22.480 --> 08:22:26.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung pwede po na maging KPI,

asr-008223
08:22:27.360 --> 08:22:32.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: yung Unified 9-1-1, yung measurable emergency outcome?

asr-008224
08:22:32.420 --> 08:22:32.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-008225
08:22:33.540 --> 08:22:34.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Noted, duly noted.

asr-008226
08:22:34.900 --> 08:22:36.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And maganda po yung suggestion yan.

asr-008227
08:22:36.640 --> 08:22:38.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Very good suggestion, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008228
08:22:39.680 --> 08:22:43.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And can the DILG agree to that?

asr-008229
08:22:43.940 --> 08:22:45.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Na isama po natin yun, sir.

asr-008230
08:22:45.160 --> 08:22:45.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, sir.

asr-008231
08:22:45.940 --> 08:22:46.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, sir.

asr-008232
08:22:48.460 --> 08:22:49.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I'll go to my next question.

asr-008233
08:22:49.780 --> 08:22:52.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, through you,

asr-008234
08:22:53.380 --> 08:22:57.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: if the real measure of 9-1-1 is timely response and life-saving,

asr-008235
08:22:57.360 --> 08:23:02.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: then hindi po sapat na mabilis dumating ang ambulansya.

asr-008236
08:23:02.560 --> 08:23:07.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pagdating ng ambulance, may trained person ba na kayang magsimulang magligtas ng buhay?

asr-008237
08:23:08.760 --> 08:23:12.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: TESDA po already has a specific paramedic training program.

asr-008238
08:23:13.620 --> 08:23:17.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, my question is, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor,

asr-008239
08:23:17.940 --> 08:23:26.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: can the Unified 9-1-1 budget be used to train LGU personnel as paramedics using these existing TESDA programs?

asr-008240
08:23:26.180 --> 08:23:26.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-008241
08:23:26.540 --> 08:23:27.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, we have one.

asr-008242
08:23:27.340 --> 08:23:32.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have 5,000 nurses nakasama po dyan under sa BFP.

asr-008243
08:23:32.560 --> 08:23:38.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, wala pong aandar na ambulansya, wala pong trained nurses na sumagip ng buhay ng ating mga mamayan.

asr-008244
08:23:39.340 --> 08:23:40.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron pong nurse, I agree to that.

asr-008245
08:23:41.140 --> 08:23:45.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ang tanong is, is that nurse qualified also as a paramedic?

asr-008246
08:23:45.420 --> 08:23:46.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Definitely, yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008247
08:23:47.600 --> 08:23:53.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, pwede po ba natin, kasi kaya ako sinasabi, meron nang existing TESDA programs.

asr-008248
08:23:54.160 --> 08:23:55.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can we tie that up?

asr-008249
08:23:55.540 --> 08:23:56.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-008250
08:23:57.340 --> 08:24:00.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The DILG is doing that already, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008251
08:24:00.140 --> 08:24:09.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, more importantly, can the DILG establish a national policy or standard that every ambulance operating as part of an LGU emergency response

asr-008252
08:24:09.900 --> 08:24:17.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or Unified 9-1-1 system should eventually have at least one properly trained and certified paramedic on board?

asr-008253
08:24:17.880 --> 08:24:22.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, Mr. Speaker, I think that's a very good question.

asr-008254
08:24:22.160 --> 08:24:25.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero lumalabas na po yan sa saklaw ng...

asr-008255
08:24:25.160 --> 08:24:27.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ng DILG.

asr-008256
08:24:28.460 --> 08:24:30.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: DILG is there to supervise.

asr-008257
08:24:30.720 --> 08:24:41.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But if we make a law regarding this, mas lalo po natin mabibigyan ngipin ang DILG and even po na sumunod, lalo na ang ating mga local government units.

asr-008258
08:24:42.540 --> 08:24:52.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kaya ako lang po binabanggit kasi, siyempre, under po kasi yung LGU emergency response dun sa mga LGU nga.

asr-008259
08:24:52.000 --> 08:24:55.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And in an emergency, siyempre, every minute counts.

asr-008260
08:24:55.160 --> 08:24:59.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung may trained paramedic sa ambulance, hindi kailangang hintayin.

asr-008261
08:25:00.100 --> 08:25:04.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Makarating sa ER bago magsimula ang proper intervention.

asr-008262
08:25:04.580 --> 08:25:11.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Habang nasa ambulance pa lang, pwede nang ma-assess, ma-stabilize, at mabigyan ng appropriate pre-hospital care ang pasyente.

asr-008263
08:25:11.980 --> 08:25:14.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi those minutes can save a life.

asr-008264
08:25:14.700 --> 08:25:18.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker, ang BFP natin are personally trained.

asr-008265
08:25:18.160 --> 08:25:23.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And actually, hindi lang po sila sila yung trained, but they're also extending training.

asr-008266
08:25:24.040 --> 08:25:25.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Lalo na po sa ating mga local.

asr-008267
08:25:25.160 --> 08:25:30.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, ang problema nito, hindi lang po ito problema ng DILG o ng BFP.

asr-008268
08:25:31.060 --> 08:25:34.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Problema po ito ng local government units.

asr-008269
08:25:34.280 --> 08:25:35.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, nagtutulungan po sila.

asr-008270
08:25:35.960 --> 08:25:40.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kaya nga po, kinukompleto natin mga fire trucks, kinukompleto natin ang fire station.

asr-008271
08:25:40.880 --> 08:25:43.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sana makompleto pa natin yung ambulances.

asr-008272
08:25:43.500 --> 08:25:49.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Lalo na pag na-release lang, 80% lang po ang inihingi na naka-earmark po para sa BFP.

asr-008273
08:25:49.980 --> 08:25:55.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Para po, mahintunin yung kaka-hingi po natin na parang nagmamakaawat tayo ng mga ambulanses.

asr-008274
08:25:55.160 --> 08:25:55.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At mga fire trucks.

asr-008275
08:25:56.100 --> 08:26:00.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Totoo yun. And I agree to that. And I fully support yung sinasabi mo, distinguished colleague.

asr-008276
08:26:01.520 --> 08:26:06.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What I'm asking is tulong naman po ito para sa unified 911 program.

asr-008277
08:26:07.140 --> 08:26:08.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kaya po, sinasuggest ko lang.

asr-008278
08:26:08.960 --> 08:26:15.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And tinatanong ko, can DILG commit to work with DESDA and DOH on a national standard?

asr-008279
08:26:15.440 --> 08:26:16.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Definitely, yes.

asr-008280
08:26:16.520 --> 08:26:22.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: With a reasonable transition period that every LGU 911 ambulance should have a trained paramedic on board?

asr-008281
08:26:22.620 --> 08:26:23.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, I totally agree.

asr-008282
08:26:23.940 --> 08:26:27.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And DILG is working on it, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008283
08:26:27.520 --> 08:26:32.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And can the 2027 911 budget be used to begin training these paramedics?

asr-008284
08:26:33.700 --> 08:26:35.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung po pwede lang po.

asr-008285
08:26:36.160 --> 08:26:43.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: If not, what specific authority or budget provision does DILG need from Congress para po magawa po natin ito?

asr-008286
08:26:46.060 --> 08:26:50.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, actually po ang mga BFP kasi natin po is NC2 trained po yan.

asr-008287
08:26:51.800 --> 08:26:53.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And well, we really need them.

asr-008288
08:26:53.940 --> 08:26:57.740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kung hindi lang po yung 911 even sa training.

asr-008289
08:26:58.280 --> 08:27:00.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But we make do of what we have.

asr-008290
08:27:01.040 --> 08:27:04.040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There are no reasons dahil kulang sa pondo, ihinto tayo.

asr-008291
08:27:04.200 --> 08:27:09.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi po yan ang patakaran ng ating Secretary Jalvik Rimulya under his leadership.

asr-008292
08:27:10.040 --> 08:27:13.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So nakita naman po natin ang response time ng police.

asr-008293
08:27:13.920 --> 08:27:16.020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nakita naman po natin ang galaw ng BFP.

asr-008294
08:27:16.700 --> 08:27:21.460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So I'm very proud and privileged to defend the DILG family.

asr-008295
08:27:21.720 --> 08:27:23.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because they are really performing well.

asr-008296
08:27:24.600 --> 08:27:27.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Lalo na po sa mga nangyari sa ating pong bansa.

asr-008297
08:27:28.180 --> 08:27:29.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero kung kulang man ang pondo,

asr-008298
08:27:30.220 --> 08:27:37.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: dyan po may sinubmit na po ang DILG family na dapat pag-usapan po dito sa plenaryo.

asr-008299
08:27:37.900 --> 08:27:40.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kung performing, I believe in meritocracy.

asr-008300
08:27:40.840 --> 08:27:44.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kung performing ang agency, dapat natin pong dagdagan.

asr-008301
08:27:44.580 --> 08:27:47.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Dahil safety po ng tao ang pinag-usapan po natin dito.

asr-008302
08:27:48.280 --> 08:27:53.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes, and I agree to that 101% distinguished sponsor.

asr-008303
08:27:53.200 --> 08:27:56.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So ang akin lang naman po ay tulong and suggestions.

asr-008304
08:27:57.060 --> 08:28:00.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Because yung current 911 program po sa Amerika,

asr-008305
08:28:00.860 --> 08:28:04.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kahit daw yung mga driver ng ambulansya,

asr-008306
08:28:04.760 --> 08:28:06.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ay may special training sa paramedic.

asr-008307
08:28:07.780 --> 08:28:12.400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ah yeah, sana po umabot tayo sa ganong level.

asr-008308
08:28:13.280 --> 08:28:15.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Okay, let me proceed to my next question.

asr-008309
08:28:17.560 --> 08:28:22.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, just one constructive question for the BJMP.

asr-008310
08:28:23.200 --> 08:28:30.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Are all eligible PDLs or persons deprived of liberty registered with PhilHealth?

asr-008311
08:28:31.280 --> 08:28:38.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And are the BJMP facilities actively linking them to YACAP accredited facilities,

asr-008312
08:28:39.380 --> 08:28:41.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: yung YACAP program po ng PhilHealth,

asr-008313
08:28:41.380 --> 08:28:44.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: so that they can access covered medicines through YACAP gamot?

asr-008314
08:28:45.280 --> 08:28:47.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: If not, what is preventing this?

asr-008315
08:28:49.720 --> 08:28:52.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Not all facilities, but nagsisimula na po.

asr-008317
08:28:53.180 --> 08:28:54.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There are some facilities already.

asr-008318
08:28:54.780 --> 08:28:59.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But I will be able to give you the specific number at the proper time,

asr-008319
08:28:59.680 --> 08:29:00.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: maybe by today, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008320
08:29:01.920 --> 08:29:04.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, thank you for that, distinguished sponsor.

asr-008321
08:29:04.640 --> 08:29:07.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can the BJMP coordinate with PhilHealth?

asr-008322
08:29:07.860 --> 08:29:10.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ang akin lang naman po ay para makabawas.

asr-008323
08:29:11.040 --> 08:29:14.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yung BJMP na kung meron silang binibili ng gamot,

asr-008324
08:29:15.680 --> 08:29:19.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: yung mga kasama na dun sa YACAP gamot at sa YACAP clinics,

asr-008325
08:29:19.560 --> 08:29:21.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ay hindi na po nila kailangan i-purchase.

asr-008326
08:29:21.280 --> 08:29:21.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

asr-008327
08:29:21.840 --> 08:29:23.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pwede na lang bilhin dun sa...

asr-008328
08:29:23.180 --> 08:29:27.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yung mga pera nila, yung mga gamot na lang na kailangan na wala dun sa YACAP gamot.

asr-008329
08:29:27.920 --> 08:29:30.240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Actually, BJMP is doing that already.

asr-008330
08:29:30.800 --> 08:29:33.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero dapat po sigurong pa-ingtingin pa,

asr-008331
08:29:33.720 --> 08:29:41.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo na ang coordination sa ating mga LGUs na may YACAP and gamot program.

asr-008332
08:29:41.820 --> 08:29:48.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, sana po ma-improve lang natin yung registration at ma-qualify natin itong mga PPS.

asr-008333
08:29:48.180 --> 08:29:50.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. It's still ongoing and gagawin po yan ng BJMP.

asr-008334
08:29:51.120 --> 08:29:51.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that.

asr-008335
08:29:51.580 --> 08:29:53.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, distinguished sponsor.

asr-008336
08:29:53.180 --> 08:29:55.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008337
08:29:55.460 --> 08:30:00.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And going to the BFP, Mr. Speaker...

asr-008338
08:30:00.440 --> 08:30:04.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We already discussed BFP extensively during the committee hearing.

asr-008339
08:30:05.140 --> 08:30:07.740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So hindi ko na puulitin yung aking detailed questions.

asr-008340
08:30:08.500 --> 08:30:13.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But the CPBRD's review of COA findings shows that as of the end of 2025,

asr-008341
08:30:14.680 --> 08:30:19.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: 100 municipalities still had no activated fire stations.

asr-008342
08:30:19.800 --> 08:30:22.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: 64 had neither a fire station or a fire truck.

asr-008343
08:30:23.340 --> 08:30:27.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And BFP had shortages of 20,854 fire coats,

asr-008344
08:30:27.780 --> 08:30:29.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: 22,019 gloves,

asr-008345
08:30:31.000 --> 08:30:34.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and 36,888 fireman's hoods.

asr-008346
08:30:35.800 --> 08:30:40.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Considering that the BFP has its regular appropriations plus fire code earmarked revenues,

asr-008347
08:30:41.700 --> 08:30:44.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: specifically available for modernization,

asr-008348
08:30:45.740 --> 08:30:48.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: may we request the BFP to submit to this representation

asr-008349
08:30:48.920 --> 08:30:54.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: a national master plan for completely closing these gaps.

asr-008350
08:30:54.700 --> 08:30:57.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For every LGU still lacking a fire station,

asr-008351
08:30:57.780 --> 08:30:59.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or fire truck,

asr-008352
08:30:59.780 --> 08:31:02.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and for every identified equipment shortage,

asr-008353
08:31:02.840 --> 08:31:04.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what is needed, how much will it cost,

asr-008354
08:31:05.480 --> 08:31:06.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what funding source,

asr-008355
08:31:07.280 --> 08:31:09.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: including yung earmarked revenues po natin,

asr-008356
08:31:09.480 --> 08:31:10.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: will be used,

asr-008357
08:31:10.580 --> 08:31:13.380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and by what year will the deficiency be eliminated?

asr-008358
08:31:14.840 --> 08:31:17.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Isa pa pong tanong ko is,

asr-008359
08:31:17.700 --> 08:31:22.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: meron po ba tayong guideline or a scientific basis

asr-008360
08:31:23.360 --> 08:31:26.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: on how many fire stations and fire trucks

asr-008361
08:31:26.360 --> 08:31:27.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: should there be,

asr-008362
08:31:27.680 --> 08:31:28.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: for example,

asr-008363
08:31:28.680 --> 08:31:32.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: pagka may one municipality na halimbawa 30 baranggays.

asr-008364
08:31:34.680 --> 08:31:38.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tapos if the units are old na,

asr-008365
08:31:38.280 --> 08:31:40.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: let's say mga 3 or 4 years old,

asr-008366
08:31:40.900 --> 08:31:43.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kailan po ba siya dapat i-replace?

asr-008367
08:31:44.060 --> 08:31:46.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kailan po ba siya nagiging obsolete?

asr-008368
08:31:47.140 --> 08:31:47.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

asr-008369
08:31:48.280 --> 08:31:49.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sinsay lang po natin, no?

asr-008370
08:31:49.740 --> 08:31:51.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So since marami po yan,

asr-008371
08:31:51.460 --> 08:31:53.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: talaga pong maraming challenges ang BFP.

asr-008372
08:31:53.560 --> 08:31:57.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I totally agree with my idol, Congressman Nazal.

asr-008373
08:31:57.680 --> 08:32:01.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's why we are asking for budget.

asr-008374
08:32:01.740 --> 08:32:04.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Na hindi naman po talaga galing sa ga'a.

asr-008375
08:32:04.580 --> 08:32:08.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang inihingi po natin yung sa fees na para po sa kanila.

asr-008376
08:32:09.040 --> 08:32:10.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because according to our data,

asr-008377
08:32:11.440 --> 08:32:13.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ang ginawa po natin pala before that,

asr-008378
08:32:13.420 --> 08:32:14.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: even last year,

asr-008379
08:32:15.160 --> 08:32:17.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: dapat po data-driven bago po magplano.

asr-008380
08:32:18.080 --> 08:32:21.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because we might be buying a thousand-gallon fire truck

asr-008381
08:32:21.660 --> 08:32:23.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pero hindi makakapasok dahil napakalaki.

asr-008382
08:32:24.280 --> 08:32:27.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So ganoon na po yung ginawa ng Bureau of Fire and Protection.

asr-008383
08:32:27.680 --> 08:32:29.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So it's not only the cleansing,

asr-008384
08:32:29.880 --> 08:32:31.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but even the planning.

asr-008385
08:32:31.640 --> 08:32:34.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But their planning is basing on the data.

asr-008386
08:32:35.360 --> 08:32:36.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And as of now,

asr-008387
08:32:36.840 --> 08:32:39.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 61 po ang kulang pa natin na fire station.

asr-008388
08:32:40.700 --> 08:32:42.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Fire trucks, 106.

asr-008389
08:32:43.280 --> 08:32:45.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And kung tatanungin niyo po, ano yung lifespan?

asr-008390
08:32:45.860 --> 08:32:46.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hanggang 20 years.

asr-008391
08:32:47.460 --> 08:32:49.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So ang inuna po talaga ng Bureau of Fire ngayon,

asr-008392
08:32:50.220 --> 08:32:52.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo na po yung mga 40-year-old na fire trucks,

asr-008393
08:32:52.540 --> 08:32:54.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: so wala pong politika,

asr-008394
08:32:55.580 --> 08:32:56.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: but depending sa necessity

asr-008395
08:32:56.540 --> 08:32:59.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ng ating local government units,

asr-008396
08:32:59.900 --> 08:33:01.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and we want this done.

asr-008397
08:33:02.020 --> 08:33:03.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: All we need is the release.

asr-008398
08:33:04.460 --> 08:33:07.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And with the supervision of our good secretary

asr-008399
08:33:07.720 --> 08:33:09.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: who cleansed the BFP,

asr-008400
08:33:10.420 --> 08:33:12.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and even going to a government-to-government,

asr-008401
08:33:13.000 --> 08:33:14.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: so mas magiging pong madali,

asr-008402
08:33:14.700 --> 08:33:15.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: magiging transparent,

asr-008403
08:33:16.300 --> 08:33:17.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and sasabi ko may accountability,

asr-008404
08:33:18.600 --> 08:33:20.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: wala pong korupsyon na pwedeng mangyari.

asr-008405
08:33:21.480 --> 08:33:22.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Government there now,

asr-008406
08:33:22.940 --> 08:33:24.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: they just went to South Korea

asr-008407
08:33:24.340 --> 08:33:26.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: two months ago or three months ago,

asr-008408
08:33:27.180 --> 08:33:29.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: so papunta na po tayo doon.

asr-008409
08:33:29.600 --> 08:33:31.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So hindi lang po paglinis na nga hanay

asr-008410
08:33:31.280 --> 08:33:32.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ng ating personnel,

asr-008411
08:33:32.960 --> 08:33:34.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: even po yung ating equipment,

asr-008412
08:33:35.300 --> 08:33:37.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and even po yung ating ambulansya,

asr-008413
08:33:37.900 --> 08:33:39.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and lahat po ng personnel,

asr-008414
08:33:39.340 --> 08:33:40.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: mga nurses natin, sinabi natin,

asr-008415
08:33:40.980 --> 08:33:42.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: NC2, very well equipped,

asr-008416
08:33:43.180 --> 08:33:45.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pero kulang pa ba kung pwede pang dagdagan ng training,

asr-008417
08:33:45.840 --> 08:33:46.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: dagdagan po natin.

asr-008418
08:33:47.620 --> 08:33:49.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So we have to think of a lot of ways.

asr-008419
08:33:49.820 --> 08:33:52.280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So these are, we know the problem,

asr-008420
08:33:52.860 --> 08:33:53.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and we know the solution.

asr-008421
08:33:54.540 --> 08:33:55.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And the solution is,

asr-008422
08:33:55.540 --> 08:33:59.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: just release 80% of the fees

asr-008423
08:33:59.980 --> 08:34:03.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: na naki-earmark po yearly sa kanila.

asr-008424
08:34:03.960 --> 08:34:05.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I fully support you on that.

asr-008425
08:34:06.020 --> 08:34:08.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yan nga po yung pinaglalaban natin lagi sa DBM,

asr-008426
08:34:08.380 --> 08:34:10.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: na dapat ang earmark ng isang ahensya

asr-008427
08:34:10.660 --> 08:34:12.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ay dapat nakukuha niya.

asr-008428
08:34:12.840 --> 08:34:14.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I would like to applaud

asr-008429
08:34:14.880 --> 08:34:18.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: the good secretary for doing a G2G

asr-008430
08:34:18.720 --> 08:34:20.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: on the Eurofire.

asr-008431
08:34:20.260 --> 08:34:21.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Just for the knowledge of everyone,

asr-008432
08:34:23.100 --> 08:34:24.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kulang po natin is,

asr-008433
08:34:24.340 --> 08:34:26.880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 40,000 personnel.

asr-008434
08:34:28.660 --> 08:34:31.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang binibigay lang po ng DBMs natin is

asr-008435
08:34:31.200 --> 08:34:33.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2,000 personnel per year.

asr-008436
08:34:34.120 --> 08:34:35.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Para masolve po natin ito,

asr-008437
08:34:35.320 --> 08:34:36.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: it will take 20 years.

asr-008438
08:34:37.320 --> 08:34:39.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So we are just asking,

asr-008439
08:34:39.340 --> 08:34:40.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: additional 2,000

asr-008440
08:34:40.580 --> 08:34:42.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: para sa sampung taon,

asr-008441
08:34:43.460 --> 08:34:45.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kumpleto na po yung ating personnel sa BFP,

asr-008442
08:34:46.520 --> 08:34:47.580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: dahil hindi lang po

asr-008443
08:34:47.580 --> 08:34:49.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: sa pagsugpo ng sunog

asr-008444
08:34:49.500 --> 08:34:50.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ang ginagawa nila.

asr-008445
08:34:51.100 --> 08:34:52.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pati po pag-rescue,

asr-008446
08:34:52.920 --> 08:34:53.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pati po 911,

asr-008447
08:34:54.060 --> 08:34:54.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: nasa BFP,

asr-008448
08:34:54.340 --> 08:34:54.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: sa kanila na.

asr-008449
08:34:55.520 --> 08:34:57.860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, kung equip po natin sila,

asr-008450
08:34:58.340 --> 08:34:59.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kung tutulungan po natin sila,

asr-008451
08:34:59.780 --> 08:35:01.780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: mas magiging maganda ang servisyo

asr-008452
08:35:01.780 --> 08:35:03.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: para sa ating mga kababayan.

asr-008453
08:35:04.720 --> 08:35:06.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-008454
08:35:06.340 --> 08:35:07.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, ang hinihingi ko na lang po is,

asr-008455
08:35:07.780 --> 08:35:10.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: can the BFP commit to submit this master plan

asr-008456
08:35:10.680 --> 08:35:12.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: with annual targets to Congress?

asr-008457
08:35:13.780 --> 08:35:14.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes,

asr-008458
08:35:14.920 --> 08:35:15.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker.

asr-008459
08:35:15.960 --> 08:35:16.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kailan mo kaya?

asr-008460
08:35:18.680 --> 08:35:20.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can we submit it by

asr-008461
08:35:20.600 --> 08:35:22.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Monday, next week?

asr-008462
08:35:22.640 --> 08:35:23.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If you don't mind.

asr-008463
08:35:23.140 --> 08:35:24.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that.

asr-008464
08:35:24.340 --> 08:35:25.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-008465
08:35:25.980 --> 08:35:28.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I fully support what you've said

asr-008466
08:35:28.320 --> 08:35:30.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: na dapat po yung earmarked funds ng

asr-008467
08:35:30.020 --> 08:35:31.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DILG at ng Bureau of Fire

asr-008468
08:35:31.820 --> 08:35:33.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ay ma-release na po sa kanila.

asr-008469
08:35:33.680 --> 08:35:34.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Maraming maraming salamat po.

asr-008470
08:35:35.840 --> 08:35:36.680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

asr-008471
08:35:37.120 --> 08:35:39.580
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Thank you, Honorable Nazal. Majority Leader.

asr-008472
08:36:01.520 --> 08:36:02.720
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Mr. Speaker.

asr-008473
08:36:02.900 --> 08:36:05.020
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Next, to interpellate the sponsor,

asr-008474
08:36:05.540 --> 08:36:06.880
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: I move to recognize

asr-008475
08:36:06.880 --> 08:36:09.000
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Representative Iris Marie

asr-008476
08:36:09.000 --> 08:36:11.700
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: de Mesa Montes of Partilis 4K.

asr-008477
08:36:12.140 --> 08:36:13.540
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Honorable Iris Marie

asr-008478
08:36:13.540 --> 08:36:15.440
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: de Mesa Montes

asr-008479
08:36:15.440 --> 08:36:16.940
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: is recognized to interpellate the sponsor.

asr-008480
08:36:16.940 --> 08:36:18.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-008481
08:36:18.840 --> 08:36:20.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The Kababaihan Kabalikatan

asr-008482
08:36:20.780 --> 08:36:22.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: para sa Kapakanan at Kaunlaran ng Bayan

asr-008483
08:36:22.800 --> 08:36:24.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: would like to direct some questions

asr-008486
08:36:24.760 --> 08:36:26.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: to the Philippine Commission on Women.

asr-008487
08:36:30.520 --> 08:36:32.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Una kong tanong,

asr-008488
08:36:32.340 --> 08:36:34.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: how much is the total estimated

asr-008489
08:36:34.520 --> 08:36:36.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 5% GAD budget

asr-008490
08:36:37.320 --> 08:36:38.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: across all

asr-008491
08:36:38.620 --> 08:36:40.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: government entities

asr-008492
08:36:40.000 --> 08:36:41.540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: for 2027?

asr-008493
08:36:43.400 --> 08:36:44.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Are we including

asr-008494
08:36:44.700 --> 08:36:45.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the LGUs, ma'am?

asr-008495
08:36:47.620 --> 08:36:50.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I don't think we have that data

asr-008496
08:36:50.520 --> 08:36:51.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: for now.

asr-008497
08:36:51.340 --> 08:36:53.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But

asr-008498
08:36:53.720 --> 08:36:56.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: aalamin po natin.

asr-008499
08:36:56.220 --> 08:36:59.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero for national government agencies na lang po,

asr-008500
08:37:00.340 --> 08:37:01.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: itanggalin na po natin

asr-008501
08:37:01.640 --> 08:37:03.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung LGUs.

